                <pb facs="0788" n="776" sameAs="frus:frus1942v01/pg776"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.248/801: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Ireland</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-12-10T18:00:00-04:00">December 10, 1942—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>157. Your 241, December 6,<anchor n="33" xml:id="d671-f1"/> and 243, December 7.
                    The friendly action of the Irish Government in this matter is greatly
                    appreciated here and we wish to commend you on your excellent handling of this
                    whole situation. Paraphrases of your telegrams have been forwarded to the War
                    Department and their attention invited particularly to your recommendation
                    regarding instructions to air crews likely to fly over Ireland.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
